# Nginx Proxy Manager access lists

## Gate

Use when the user authorized NPM work and the turn needs **access lists**
(IP allow/deny clients, optional HTTP basic auth satisy rules). Host-only or
SSL-only asks → other rules. Removing restrictions / deleting lists → also
`nginx-proxy-manager-safety`.

## Transport

No NPM MCP discovered. Prefer REST API on operator-resolved `BASE` with
Bearer auth, or admin UI. **Do not invent MCP tool names.**

## API map (HTTP)

| Need | Method + path |
| --- | --- |
| List access lists | `GET /api/nginx/access-lists` |
| One access list | `GET /api/nginx/access-lists/{id}` |
| Create access list | `POST /api/nginx/access-lists` |
| Update access list | `PUT /api/nginx/access-lists/{id}` |
| Delete access list | `DELETE /api/nginx/access-lists/{id}` (safety gate) |

Attach to a proxy host via host update (`access_list_id`) after both ids are
resolved (`nginx-proxy-manager-hosts`).

## Craft fields (typical)

Confirm field names from a live get on this instance:

- **name** — human label
- **clients** — directive + address (allow/deny + CIDR or IP)
- **items** / auth items — basic-auth usernames; **never** put passwords in
  chat — set via UI/API with operator-provided secret channel
- **satisfy_any** — whether any client/auth match passes

## Discover first

1. Never invent access-list ids — list/resolve this turn.
2. Before widening (adding allow-all, removing deny, clearing auth), show the
   current clients/auth summary from get evidence.
3. Before attach/detach on a host, prove host id + access_list id.

## Defaults

1. Prefer update-in-place of an existing list over delete+recreate.
2. Tightening access (adding deny, removing public allow) is fine with an
   ordinary update verb naming the list.
3. **Widening** access (0.0.0.0/0 allow, drop auth, satisfy_any that opens
   the door) needs an explicit widen/open verb per `nginx-proxy-manager-safety`.
4. Receipts: id + name + client count / auth user count — no password hashes.

## Report shape

- **id** + **name**
- **clients** summary (count + whether any public allow)
- **auth** — username list only
- **hosts using this list** when known from host inventory

## Related (this plugin)

- `nginx-proxy-manager-hosts` — attach access_list_id
- `nginx-proxy-manager-safety` — widen / delete gates
